extraction_notes: "THE TWO TYPES ARE `variants`, AND THIS IS THE FIRST CLASS IN THIS BOOK TO USE `skills_additional` - the mechanism BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F31 shipped in PR #834. The base class is the Peacemaker and carries NO hand to hand at all, which is what the book''s skill list prints. The Fire and Brimstone variant adds Hand to Hand: Basic and one more W.P., and carries the extra +10 S.D.C. the book gives it. Its `bonuses` block restates the shared combat and save figures because a variant''s bonuses REPLACE rather than merge. The alcohol tolerance is Fire and Brimstone only and is an ability rather than a bonus, since there is no drunkenness mechanic to attach it to. THE +1D4+2 TO M.A. IS NOT STORED AS A NUMBER: `bonuses.attributes` takes a fixed value and a dice expression there is not applied, so it is an ability to be rolled at creation - the same call the Saddle Tramp and the Wired Gunslinger needed. Literacy and Math are printed as flat 98% with no per-level gain, unlike every other skill on the list, and are stored that way. Standard Equipment stores only the catalog rows that exist; the book also lists light to medium M.D.C. body armour, a hooded travelling robe, two sets of white or grey silk robes for sermons, a quality cowboy hat, boots, sunglasses, tinted goggles, a megaphone, a notepad and pens, a post-Rifts Bible, a large wooden cross, a silver cross on a chain, six wooden stakes and a mallet, a magnifying glass, a pocket translator, a first-aid kit, an RMKS Robot Medical Kit, a bottle of wine, matches, a pocket mirror, a pair of handcuffs, 50 ft of rope, and two weapons of choice with three spare clips each. The book notes some Preachers, especially Fire and Brimstone ones, carry electric stunners. It also records that no self-respecting town will fail to give a Preacher a room, meals and laundry, which is why the purse is small."
